! I-Box 4 diagnostic program (docs/jb_ax4b_ibox-4.pdf p.155, routine
! 150 "----1250---CB AND CBR TEST", the IBR1-IBR9 block) -- the plain
! "CB" mnemonic (Count and Branch, v=00/refill=0/branch-if-nonzero),
! part of the CB/CBR family docs/archival_inventory.md flagged as
! "the largest, most regression-test-shaped block" in I-Box 1's own
! inventory entry and, for this document, "large and self-contained"
! (I-Box 4's own entry). Exercises StretchExecute.bsv's CountBranch
! arm end to end: `take = (branchIfZero==1) ? (newCount==0) :
! (newCount!=0)`, decode's `branchIfZero`/`v`/`refill` bit extraction
! (StretchDecode.bsv tryCountBranch), and confirms v=00 truly leaves
! the value field alone (no accidental write).
!
! Mnemonic-table note: "CB" was, before this program, the only Count-
! -and-Branch mnemonic this assembler encoded (v/refill/bz always
! zero, matching StretchSmoke.bsv's own hand-assembled usage -- see
! strap_asm.py's prior module-docstring wording). Reading this
! section's source revealed the full CB[R][Z][H|+|-] mnemonic family
! (16 variants, matching I-Box 1's own "16-variant CB/CBR family"
! description); the encoder (enc_count_branch) already accepted the
! full (v, refill, bz) parameter space, and StretchExecute.bsv's
! CountBranch arm already consults all three fields end to end
! (confirmed by reading the whole arm before adding anything -- see
! docs/archival_inventory.md for the reasoning), so this was a mnemonic
! table addition, not new model or decode work. Table added to
! opcodes.py (CB_CODES), sourced from the pocket card's own "INDEX
! BRANCHING" legend and cross-checked against real occurrences in this
! section (CB/CB+/CBH/CB- on this page, CBR/CBR+ on p.159, CBRZH/CBRZ-
! on p.165) -- not inferred from listing usage alone (the mistake this
! project corrected twice already for the SIC finding). A companion
! finding, also from this reading pass: section 138 (Refill/RCZ, the
! *other* I-Box 4 candidate) was rejected outright -- its every check
! depends on a `$R` system symbol this assembler doesn't recognize and
! whose meaning isn't recoverable from the listing alone; see
! docs/archival_inventory.md.
!
! Source transcription note: the original routine's own instructions
! (LX,$X1,IBRA1 / four CB,$X1,<next> / SX,$X1,IBR8 / B,IBR8) are
! reproduced faithfully in kind -- same XW-literal setup (VALUE/COUNT/
! REFILL fields), same four chained CB instructions decrementing one
! shared index register's count from 4 to 0, branching on the first
! three and falling through on the fourth ("COUNT TO ZERO NO BRANCH",
! the source's own comment). What is NOT reproduced is the source's
! own pass/fail SIGNALING mechanism: on real hardware, a failed branch
! falls into a `BD,CBERAn` (Branch Disabled -- a deliberate hang,
! meant for a human at the console to notice) or, for the value test,
! self-modifies a NOP placeholder at IBR8 into a "BD,IBR9" instruction
! by storing X1's own packed IndexWord and depending on VALUE's bit-
! position happening to line up with the BranchOrMisc format's ADDRESS
! field -- a self-modifying-code idiom this project has previously
! flagged as a structural dependency (I-Box 4's section 148 needs SVA
! for a similar reason) and not worth reproducing bit-for-bit here
! when the same coverage is available more simply. Instead, exactly
! like ibox1_wen_ven_indicators.strap: each of the first three CB's
! PASS path (branch taken) writes a distinctive marker (100, via LVI)
! into its own pre-cleared (0) index register, and the fourth CB's
! FAIL path (branch taken when it should NOT be) writes its own
! marker -- so all four branch decisions are independently checked,
! both directions covered by construction (three "should branch" and
! one "should not"), without needing SIC, self-modifying code, or a
! console operator. X1's own final state (count=0, value untouched)
! is checked directly by the testbench instead of being routed through
! a self-modified instruction.
!
! Verified non-vacuous by deliberately flipping the branch-condition
! sense in StretchExecute.bsv's CountBranch arm (`take = (branchIfZero
! == 1) ? (newCount != 0) : (newCount == 0)` -- the exact opposite of
! the real logic), rebuilding, and confirming the four branch-decision
! assertions (X2-X5) then fail: X2-X4 stay at their fail value 0 (the
! first three branches, which should fire, no longer do), and X5 gets
! written to 100 (the fourth branch, which should NOT fire, now
! wrongly does). X1_final itself still PASSES under this injected bug
! -- expected, since the bug only changes which branch fires, not the
! count/value arithmetic, so X1's final state (count=0, value=999) is
! invariant to it; X1_final is not covered by this or any other
! bug-injection round run so far, though it is still a real check (it
! pins v=00 leaving the value field alone). Reverted and confirmed
! `git diff` on StretchExecute.bsv is empty before committing. Note
! also that X1_final's expected value (0x3e70000000000) is derived by
! hand from the same packIndexWord bit layout the model itself uses
! (StretchTypes.bsv), not from an independent oracle -- a
! self-consistent check standing in for the source's own value test,
! not proof the model's packing matches real 7030 hardware.

START   LX, $1, CTL         !X1 = XW literal VALUE=999,COUNT=4,REFILL=0
        LVI, $2, 0.0        !X2 = 0 (fail marker: step 1, count 4->3, not taken)
        LVI, $3, 0.0        !X3 = 0 (fail marker: step 2, count 3->2, not taken)
        LVI, $4, 0.0        !X4 = 0 (fail marker: step 3, count 2->1, not taken)
        LVI, $5, 0.0        !X5 = 0 (fail marker: step 4, count 1->0, WAS taken -- bug)

        CB, $1, S1OK        !IBR1 -COUNT TO 3 + BRANCH
        B, S1DONE
S1OK    LVI, $2, 100
S1DONE  CB, $1, S2OK        !IBR2 -COUNT TO 2 + BRANCH
        B, S2DONE
S2OK    LVI, $3, 100
S2DONE  CB, $1, S3OK        !IBR3 -COUNT TO 1 + BRANCH
        B, S3DONE
S3OK    LVI, $4, 100
S3DONE  CB, $1, S4BUG       !IBR4 -COUNT TO ZERO NO BRANCH
        B, DONE
S4BUG   LVI, $5, 100        !reached only if the branch wrongly fired at count=0

DONE    BEW, $              !halt -- X1 checked externally: count=0, value=999 (unchanged)

CTL     XW, 999, 4, 0       !VALUE=999 (distinctive, unrelated to any address in
                            !this program), COUNT=4, REFILL=0 (never read: this
                            !block's CB instructions all carry refill=0)

        END, START
